{"title":"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute scalene triangle with no angle equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e6bc175e2a4591ad2167ca267da27cb065adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> be the equilateral triangle with three vertices on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, one of which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ffb8fae480f25fbfb60dd7b827ea225e81b7f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> be the line through the two vertices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e6bc175e2a4591ad2167ca267da27cb065adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2fd23bec5a71f3bc7898f703bd261ea0d1ea96f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/3856ff459e8e0f763e995fae8680728ba30beef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> be defined analogously. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ffb8fae480f25fbfb60dd7b827ea225e81b7f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/3856ff459e8e0f763e995fae8680728ba30beef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b686e282112ee7338ebaf3427727ac8141c10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /> be the triangle formed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ffb8fae480f25fbfb60dd7b827ea225e81b7f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/3856ff459e8e0f763e995fae8680728ba30beef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />, and the tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/620bb149eedce7c8570c99aafa2a8834e51fcc17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AYZ$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> and the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b686e282112ee7338ebaf3427727ac8141c10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /> are tangent.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We establish a complex plane with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> being the unit circle, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/2/1628b2ca090e9820e9c91c439e18f6cefd3ae321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert a\\rvert=1,\\lvert b\\rvert=1,\\lvert c\\rvert=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" /> represent points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9874ea56cf8fec1bd246793224fbcfaad17ab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2fa17f62805829f663e3bdb4763632e41a58ebb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1=e^{i\\frac{2\\pi}{3}}b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/542b7508924313db1c36440fef5dc1041d1c12dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_2=e^{i\\frac{4\\pi}{3}}b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"22\" /> be points from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc4b072ddd441d3ee2a8d59e022b4ebabc90d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega\\cap\\ell_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. Also, note that we can assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9cad1930f996ba60fac2bbee2c34d0ba212dead5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\sqrt{bc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"21\" /> representing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/e/8ced08d836dfd4e33b54e0ed0112a6061e71ed80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> be the tangent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/2070e135d74304b1ae916db2e32f4d3254640d54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1\\cdot B_2=b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3dfbdf7b0cf1a98f05fae56c221beb2b199098a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1+B_2=-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" />, we obtain the following equations:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\ell_B&amp;: z+b^2 \\overline{z}=-b\\\\\n\\ell_C&amp;: z+c^2 \\overline{z}=-c\\\\\nAB&amp;: z+ab\\overline{z}=a+b\\\\\nAC&amp;: z+ac\\overline{z}=a+c\\\\\nT_N&amp;: z+bc\\overline{z}=2\\sqrt{bc}\n\\end{align*}\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/334fc9a1d84d47227ef36e62b14c286688ac8cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D,E,F,Y,Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/3/6b335d9c18d3f4d6b28afd41d7ab14d376cf0439.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d=\\frac{b(c+2n)}{b-c},\\quad e=\\frac{c(b+2n)}{c-b},\\quad f=-\\frac{bc}{b+c}\\]\" width=\"356\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc6733d70070b8351538829c2a150c331a9895c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\frac{b(ab+bc+ca)}{b^2-ac},\\quad z=\\frac{c(ab+bc+ca)}{c^2-ab}\\]\" width=\"332\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/b/38bca9a55c0bea20b9850eb336432002b86450e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overline{y}=-\\frac{a+b+c}{b^2-ac},\\quad\\overline{z}=-\\frac{a+b+c}{c^2-ab}\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"37\" />\nWe proceed by determining the incenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b686e282112ee7338ebaf3427727ac8141c10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" />. Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/7/b9797e0683c85263bff162d9c7917054d19f6dcf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lvert d-f\\rvert=\\left\\lvert \\frac{2n(n^2+nc+c^2)}{b^2-c^2}\\right\\rvert =\\left\\lvert \\frac{2n(n+b+c)}{b^2-c^2}\\right\\rvert\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"44\" />\nBy symmetry, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61cb7208b422f66ace622bf773312ad2efd386c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert d-f\\rvert=\\lvert e-f\\rvert$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />. Also, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a19690e3b402aa17ad40eec4537a66730fd95fa1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lvert d-e\\rvert=\\left\\lvert \\frac{2bc+2nc+2nb}{b-c}\\right\\rvert=\\left\\lvert \\frac{2n(n+b+c)}{b-c}\\right\\rvert\\]\" width=\"356\" height=\"44\" />\nWe see that the ratio of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/a/78a455ffbd7b4c2fa3f272c8b8c80e72aa619edc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$de$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to the other legs in the same isosceles triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/669f10dd87e2d435839f6150b84348ae342bba64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert b+c\\rvert=\\sqrt{(b+c)\\left(\\overline{b}+\\overline{c}\\right)}=\\frac{b+c}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"267\" height=\"39\" />. Thus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/8200bb93f7071070249382aabd7e1fd043f14c4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[I=\\frac{d+e+\\frac{b+c}{n}\\cdot f}{1+1+\\frac{b+c}{n}}=\\frac{bc}{2n+b+c}\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"48\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the inradius of the same circle. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93eecd32cf7751497b2cef3e9b4cd87fac9c847b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=\\left\\lvert\\frac{n^2}{2n+b+c}-n\\right\\rvert=\\left\\lvert\\frac{n+b+c}{2n+b+c}\\right\\rvert\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"44\" />\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93ec4f1ee59bce5745be39d3780275fd255e01ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{n+b+c}{2n+b+c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"119\" height=\"41\" /> because in that case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a47a2382cb231f4aea20e89bccc69d7f02209a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\overline{r}\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63dca0858f430e2c347a09ea98494e66e0612ec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ayz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca77b9bde39f8d19ec42c7c0c740d1a99fff89b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lvert O-a\\rvert=\\lvert O-y\\rvert=\\lvert O-z\\rvert=R\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"18\" />\nSquaring gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd584aeb680b249f6b624f19292e48e9ade4f23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O\\overline{O}-a\\overline{O}-\\overline{a}O+1=R^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"200\" height=\"19\" />. By symmetry, we get\n\\begin{align*}\n(y-a)\\overline{O}+(\\overline{y}-\\overline{a})O=y\\overline{y}-1\\\\\n(z-a)\\overline{O}+(\\overline{z}-\\overline{a})O=z\\overline{z}-1\n\\end{align*}\nNote that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdca7204514616b9154fc7a2e39bb48cf6a97a0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b(a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca)+(b^2-ac)^2=(a^2+ab+b^2)(b^2+bc+c^2)\\]\" width=\"535\" height=\"20\" />\nIt follows that\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{c(a^2+ab+b^2)}{b^2-ac}\\overline{O}-\\frac{a^2+ab+b^2}{a(b^2-ac)}O=-\\frac{(a^2+ab+b^2)(b^2+bc+c^2)}{(b^2-ac)^2}\\\\\n\\frac{b(a^2+ac+c^2)}{c^2-ab}\\overline{O}-\\frac{a^2+ac+c^2}{a(c^2-ab)}O=-\\frac{(a^2+ac+c^2)(b^2+bc+c^2)}{(c^2-ab)^2}\\\\\n\\end{align*}\nSolving yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a23da84e730cbcbf8efa2fae56dd0600f6f606.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overline{O}=-\\frac{(a+b+c)(b^2+bc+c^2)}{(b^2-ac)(c^2-ab)},\\quad O=-\\frac{a(ab+bc+ca)(b^2+bc+c^2)}{(b^2-ac)(c^2-ab)}\\]\" width=\"549\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Note that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/7/a871026730e4ae070944caa3fa859bc34b222611.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(ab+bc+ca)(b^2+bc+c^2)+(b^2-ac)(c^2-ab)=bc(a+b+c)^2\\]\" width=\"503\" height=\"20\" />\nThe circumradius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> evaluates to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/4/024c7f3d55bbaf2eb5e6c6fd15ecb0436a49d149.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R=\\lvert O-a\\rvert=\\left\\lvert \\frac{bc(a+b+c)^2}{(b^2-ac)(c^2-ab)}\\right\\rvert\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"44\" />\nAnd\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0dfab69bd5742084f003ba8525d37ab8fb25a70d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R^2=\\frac{bc(a+b+c)^2}{(b^2-ac)(c^2-ab)}\\cdot\\frac{\\frac{1}{bc}(\\frac{1}{a}+\\frac{1}{b}+\\frac{1}{c})^2}{\\left(\\frac{1}{b^2}-\\frac{1}{ac}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{c^2}-\\frac{1}{ab}\\right)}\\cdot\\frac{a^2b^3c^3}{a^2b^3c^3}=\\frac{bc(a+b+c)^2(ab+bc+ca)^2}{(b^2-ac)^2(c^2-ab)^2}\\]\" width=\"650\" height=\"48\" />\nTherefore, with\n\\begin{gather*}\nO=\\frac{-a(b^2+bc+c^2)(ab+bc+ca)}{(b^2-ac)(c^2-ab)},\\quad I=\\frac{bc}{2n+b+c},\\\\\nR=\\frac{n(a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca)}{(b^2-ac)(c^2-ab)},\\quad r=\\frac{n+b+c}{2n+b+c},\n\\end{gather*}\nit is enough to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b311e4005ed0807eeb0f515b3f0d88a5a135ad6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert O-I\\rvert = \\lvert R-r\\rvert\\iff (O-I)(\\overline{O}-\\overline{I})=(R-r)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"402\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>We make the following substitutions:\n\\begin{gather*}\nS=b+c, \\quad U=a+b+c,\\quad V=ab+bc+ca,\\\\\nX=b^2+bc+c^2,\\quad P=2n+b+c,\\quad Q=(b^2-ac)(c^2-ab)\n\\end{gather*}\nSubstituting, we wish to prove that\n\\begin{gather*}\n\\left(-\\frac{aXV}{Q}-\\frac{n^2}{P}\\right)\\left(-\\frac{UX}{Q}-\\frac{1}{P}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{nUV}{Q}-\\frac{n+S}{P}\\right)^2\\iff\\\\\n(aXVP+n^2Q)(UXP+Q)=(nUVP-(n+S)Q)^2\\iff\\\\\nUVP^2(aX^2-n^2UV)+PQ(X(n^2U+aV)+2n(n+S)UV)+(n^2-(n+S)^2)Q^2=0\\tag{1}\n\\end{gather*}\nTo simplify, we express each variable in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/758272a6e19d436393c807156803e3bda1ebf3c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,S,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />:\n\\begin{gather*}\nU=a+S,\\quad V=n^2+aS,\\quad X=S^2-n^2\\\\\nP=2n+S,\\quad Q=b^2c^2-a(b^3+c^3)+a^2bc=n^4-aS^3+3an^2S+a^2n^2\n\\end{gather*}\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a47da839d2488664a60f8040fef65919752b1e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-(n+S)^2=-2nS-S^2=-PS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"287\" height=\"21\" />. Also,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a15dc9b91507fe37bf7f91a53144f7f1592c979.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[aX^2-n^2UV=a(S^4-2S^2n^2+n^4)-n^2(aS^2+a^2S+n^2S+an^2)=-S(n^4-aS^3+3an^2S+a^2n^2)=-SQ\\]\" width=\"765\" height=\"20\" />\nSubstituting the two coefficients back to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> yields\n\\begin{gather*}\n-SUVP^2Q+PQ(X(n^2U+aV)+2n(n+S)UV)-SPQ^2=0\\iff\\\\\nX(n^2U+aV)+(2n^2+2nS-PS)UV-SQ=0\\iff\\\\\nX(n^2U+aV)+(2n^2-S^2)UV-SQ=0\n\\end{gather*}\nExpanding, we have\n\\begin{align*}\nX(n^2U+aV)&amp;=2an^2S^2+n^2S^3+a^2S^3-2an^4-n^4S-a^2n^2S\\\\\n(2n^2-S^2)UV&amp;=2an^2S^2+2n^4S+2a^2n^2S+2an^4-aS^4-a^2S^3-n^2S^3-an^2S^2\\\\\n-SQ&amp;=-n^4S+aS^4-3an^2S^2-a^2n^2S\n\\end{align*}\nThose terms cancel when added, as desired.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO\" title=\"2026 USAMO\">2026 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018000508\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 404/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13910/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.055      1 -total\n 56.21%    6.776      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 42.07%    5.072      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36113:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018000508 and revision id 291568. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}